<title>CHINA: CHINA LOAN TO THAILAND TO BE AT MARKET RATES.</title>
<headline>CHINA LOAN TO THAILAND TO BE AT MARKET RATES.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest on China's pledged $1 billion contribution to an international loan package for Thailand will be calculated at market rates, the official Xinhua news agency said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Central bank governor Dai Xianglong said he notified the International Monetary Fund late on Wednesday that China would be part of a $16 billion IMF-led loan package aimed at helping Thailand out of its current economic crisis.</p>
<p>China's $1 billion in loans would have terms of three to five years and would generate interest calculated at market rates, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>It gave no further details.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.3 yuan)</p>
